---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="LoopLogic Privacy Policy — scubadeving"
  description="Privacy policy for LoopLogic. Your records stay on your device — no account, no cloud, no tracking. Android release builds send crash reports; alpha-testing forms and chat are covered too."
  ogImage="/og-looplogic.png"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-24">

    <Header showBack={true} />

    <main>
      <section class="mb-16">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
          LoopLogic Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated: October 2026</p>
      </section>

      <div class="mb-24 space-y-12">

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            Summary
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            This policy covers two things: the LoopLogic app, and the alpha-testing programme around it (forms, community chat and tester builds). The app keeps your records on your device and has no account. The testing programme does collect some personal data, described below.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            The app: data collection
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            LoopLogic does not collect, transmit, or store your records on external servers. The app requires no account or sign-in of any kind. Alerts are generated by the app on your device, not sent from a server.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            The app: on-device storage
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            All data you enter — dive checklists, O₂ cell records, scrubber logs, gas math inputs — is stored locally on your device using an on-device database. This data does not leave your device and is not accessible to scubadeving or any third party.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            Uninstalling the app removes all stored data from your device.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            The app: crash reports
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            Android release builds include <strong class="font-medium text-ink">Firebase Crashlytics</strong>. When the app crashes, it sends the crash stack trace, the app version, your device model and operating system version, the state of the device at that moment, and a randomly generated installation identifier. We do not add your name or email, and the app has no account to link a report to. We use it only to find and fix crashes. There is currently no setting in the app to turn crash reports off.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            The iOS app does not send crash reports at this time. If that changes, this policy will be updated before it does.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            The app: third-party SDKs
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            LoopLogic does not include advertising or analytics SDKs. Firebase Analytics is deliberately excluded.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            The app: permissions
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            LoopLogic does not request access to your location, camera, microphone, or contacts.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            The app may ask for the <strong class="font-medium text-ink">notification permission</strong> (Android 13 and later, and iOS) to deliver alerts for scrubber capacity, O₂ cell expiry and, on Android, CNS exposure. This permission is optional — the app is fully functional without it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            Alpha testing: forms
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            If you fill in one of our forms, we receive what you type. The interest form asks for your name, email address, the rebreather you dive, your platform, and your device and operating system version. The bug report form requires you to sign in with a Google account, because it accepts file uploads, and Google tells us the email address of that account. The feature request and exit survey forms ask for a name and email address only if you choose to give them. We use this to run the alpha, to reply to you and to decide what to build. The forms are provided by Google (Google Forms), which processes your answers under its own terms and privacy policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            Alpha testing: community chat
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            If you join our Discord server, Discord processes your account details and messages under its own terms and privacy policy. We can see what you post there.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            Alpha testing: tester builds
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            Android alpha builds are distributed with Firebase App Distribution, which processes the email address we invite. iOS alpha builds are distributed with Apple's TestFlight, which processes the email address of your Apple ID. We use the address only to give you the build.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            Keeping and deleting what we hold
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            We keep form answers and tester email addresses until the alpha ends, or until you ask us to delete them, whichever comes first. To ask, email us at the address below and we will delete what we hold within 30 days. This does not cover what Google, Discord, Apple or Firebase hold under their own policies.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            Contact
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            For privacy questions or deletion requests, contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@scubadeving.com" class="rounded underline text-accent transition-colors focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent">hello@scubadeving.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />

  </div>
</Layout>
